**What changed:** `/app/solution.sparql` — a SPARQL query returning `?professorName` and `?countries` for full professors who (1) hold a `"Professor …"` role (excluding assistant/associate strings), (2) work in at least one department of a university in an EU-27 country (list checked as of 2025-08-16, so `CH` and `US` are out), and (3) work in at least one department with >10 students currently enrolled in courses taught there — "currently" meaning `hasEnrollmentDate <= 2025-08-16` and (`hasGraduationDate` absent or `> 2025-08-16`), counted as distinct students per department.

**The check that shows it works:** run from the saved file against `/app/university_graph.ttl` with rdflib, it executes and returns

```
Orfeas Menis     | US, GR
Pepe Attanasio   | PT, GR
Aristotle Tympas | GR
```

anon — the department counts the filter relies on are `ComputerScience_NTUA 12`, `HistoryAndPhilosophy_NKUA 12`, `Engineering_Berkeley 11`, `Biology_MIT 7`, `Mathematics_Sorbonne 6`. Berkeley's 11 doesn't help anyone (US), Sorbonne's 6 excludes Marie Dubois, and MIT's 7 plus its US location exclude John Smith; Athanasios Voulodimos and Stefan Mueller are assistant professors.

**One thing worth flagging:** my first draft filtered the EU condition on the *output* `?country` variable, which silently narrowed `?countries` to EU-only (Menis came back `GR` instead of `GR, US`). That's fixed by putting the EU test in its own `SELECT DISTINCT` sub-select over `?euCountry`, so the reported country list stays complete.

Nothing left undone; `/app` contains only `university_graph.ttl` and `solution.sparql`.

